## Third-party connector brand icons

Shipped connector manifests in `packages/polyfill-connectors/manifests/` each
declare a small brand glyph (`brand.icon`, under `manifests/icons/*.svg`) to
identify the third-party service the connector connects to (e.g. Amazon,
GitHub, Spotify). All product names, trademarks, and registered trademarks
referenced or depicted by these icons are the property of their respective
owners. These icons are used by the PDP-Connect project strictly to identify
the products and companies a connector integrates with; their use implies no
sponsorship, affiliation, or endorsement by the mark holder.

A connector manifest with no legitimately available brand mark should not
carry an invented or unofficial logo. Consumers of this package's
`connector-index.json` render a deterministic monogram (the connector's
initial(s) and a color derived from its name) as the correct default for
that case — this is a normal, first-class fallback, not an error state.

This bundle also contains third-party packages, found in the esbuild metafile of the build.
Each package's own license and notice files follow.

